Pros and Cons
The main pro is that this game plays like an updated version of Deus Ex Human Revolution:
- graphically superior to DXHR (models with greater detail, PBR texturing, realistic lighting etc.);
- the same 'hacking' minigame has been made more exciting;
- expansive 'hub' areas to explore (I've spent 6+ hours methodically working through Prague and still have more than half of it to do).
Cons:
- 'Breach' mode is pointless and adds nothing to the DX universe (I played it for 5 mins to test my graphics settings before starting the game proper, won't be going back);
- the story introduces too many factions at once, in the first mission Adam is working for special ops
Duncan MacReady, then in the next scene he's rendezvousing with resistance fighter
Alex Vega, and 4 missions later I still have no idea what Adam's working toward.
Smaller niggles include:
-
PATCHED;
-
PATCHED;
- the game's title inexplicably includes a gender binary term (should be Humanity rather than Mankind);
- some of the game's dialogue contains slurs against people with mental health problems (a "madman" caused the Panchaea incident, that incident caused augmented people to become "schizos" and "psychotic killers") - as well as being unnecessarily discriminatory it is terminologically incorrect (homicidal behaviour and criminal activity ≠ psychoticism or schizophrenia).
In summary, if you enjoyed DXHR, you'll enjoy this. Re the microtransactions, I'm 8 hours in and haven't come across any gated content yet nor any prompts to spend any money, so I don't have an opinion on that.

