So some stuff about how long and much I've been waiting for this game. I remember I saw the Akuma reveal trailer in twitch mobile quality after a church service with my phone (King of Iron Fist Tournament 2015). Watched almost every tournament on twitch when I got the chance. Literally skipped the elections entirely to watch a T7 stream (Proof:
). Went to SCR 2016 just to try it out on set ups provided by Namco. And when "Early 2017" struck, I counted the days till release. There hasn't been a fighting game that has gotten me this invested into it and I  can't say it hasn't been a journey or some♥♥♥♥♥♥lol. That being said I am glad sooo many people are finally giving Tekken a chance if they haven't already and I love all of you for enjoying this game as much as I am.
TLDR: The anticipation was too much and the wait was well worth it. 7/7

